speechtext:
Yes, I think that is true;
it is to effect conformity with section 67 and with section 72.
Motion agreed to; amendments read the second time and concurred in.

That is not the case;
if the hon. gentleman will look at clause 6 the situation is just the reverse: the farmer makes the proposal. Clause 6 reads:
A farmer who is unable to meet his liabilities as they become due.
There are other provisions to which reference was made the other day, but the basis of the foundation of jurisdiction is that the farmer makes an application for a composition.
